  "missionSputnik1": "The first artificial satellite. This metal ball, about the size of a beach ball, circled Earth for about three months. Its beeping could be heard on radios and it started the space age.",
  "missionVostok1": "Yuri Gagarin became the first person in space. He circled Earth once, in about 108 minutes.",
  "missionApollo11": "Neil Armstrong and Buzz Aldrin landed in the Sea of Tranquility and became the first people to walk on the Moon. Michael Collins waited for them in orbit.",
  "missionVenera7": "The first spacecraft to land on another planet and send a signal back. It sent data from Venus for about 23 minutes in the crushing heat.",
  "missionViking1": "It landed on Mars and worked there for more than six years, sending the first long series of photos and weather reports from the surface of another planet.",
  "missionVoyager1": "Launched in 1977, it flew past Jupiter and Saturn and entered interstellar space in 2012. It is the farthest human-made object from Earth.",
  "missionHubble": "Launched in 1990, it looks at the universe from above Earth's air. Its sharp pictures helped measure the age of the universe and showed thousands of faraway galaxies.",
  "missionHuygens": "Huygens, a probe carried by Cassini, parachuted down to Saturn's moon Titan. It was the first landing in the outer solar system, and it sent pictures from the surface.",
  "missionCuriosity": "This car-sized rover landed in Gale Crater using a rocket-powered sky crane. It found that Mars once had the right conditions for life.",
  "missionMangalyaan": "India's Mars Orbiter Mission reached Mars orbit on its first try, a first for any country, and at a very low cost.",
  "missionRosetta": "Rosetta's lander Philae touched down on comet 67P/Churyumov–Gerasimenko, the first landing on a comet. Rosetta itself circled the comet for two years.",
  "missionNewhorizons": "After a nine-year trip, it flew past Pluto and showed us icy mountains and a huge heart-shaped plain for the first time.",
  "missionPerseverance": "The Perseverance rover landed in Jezero Crater to look for signs of old life and collect rock samples. Its helicopter Ingenuity made the first powered flight on another planet.",
  "missionJwst": "The largest space telescope has a 6.5-metre gold mirror and watches the sky in infrared light from 1.5 million km away. It sees some of the first galaxies.",
  "missionChandrayaan3": "India became the fourth country to land softly on the Moon, and the first near its south pole. The Vikram lander carried the Pragyan rover.",
